==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries allows the model to generate two AuditEntries with the same (auditApp, eventType) pair. The injected violation forces exactly that state, so AppendOnly and the audit completeness assertions find a counterexample: the 'one ae' cardinality in AuditCompleteness becomes false when there are two submitted-event entries for the same application.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete, AuditCompleteness
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing F_OnePendingPerCustomer allows two distinct LoanApplications for the same customer both to have status PendingReview. The injected violation forces this instance to exist, directly violating FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeciderIsStaff  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DeciderIsStaff.als
    rationale: Removing F_DeciderIsStaff permits a Decision whose decidedBy user has CustomerRole. The injected violation forces a Decision made by a customer-role user, directly falsifying FR_009_DecisionReasonAndStaffOnly (which requires all deciders to be BankStaffRole) and exposing the LeastPrivilege violation that customers should not be able to post decisions.
    expected to FAIL: FR_009_DecisionReasonAndStaffOnly, LeastPrivilege, FR_015_RoleBasedAccess
      - FR_009_DecisionReasonAndStaffOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_RoleBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication.als
    rationale: Removing F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication allows two Decision atoms to point at the same LoanApplication, modelling a double-decision race. The injected violation forces this state, which is exactly what ConcurrencySafety and FR_011_DecisionImmutability are meant to exclude.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_011_DecisionImmutability, FR_012_NoConcurrentDecisions
      - ConcurrencySafety: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_011_DecisionImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_NoConcurrentDecisions: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorAttribution  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditActorAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditActorAttribution allows audit entries to record an actor whose role does not match the event type — e.g., a bank staff member as actor on a SubmittedEvt, or a customer as actor on an ApprovedEvt. The injected violation creates a SubmittedEvt entry whose actor is a BankStaffRole user, falsifying AttributionCorrectness.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionMatrix leaves the Allowed relation unconstrained. The injected violation adds the forbidden cell CustomerRole->PostDecision, directly falsifying LeastPrivilege and FR_015_RoleBasedAccess, and also breaks PermissionCompleteness (cardinality check fails) and PermissionGrounding (extra ungrounded cell present).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionCompleteness, PermissionGrounding, FR_015_RoleBasedAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_RoleBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

